      "description": "The burn, the pixel floors and ceilings, the linger and the cost, by quality (low, medium, high). A pattern's rate is how often a point of the ribbon sees a feature pass, in Hz: 0.9 or slower (0.55 under Reduce flashing), inside Legal's 2 Hz and 1.5 Hz. glow_cap keeps a colour from reaching white. life_s is at least 2 s, so no point can rise and fall inside a second. wide_k is the alpha share a ribbon keeps once it is wide on screen (from wide_from to wide_to times its pixel floor): the flash reading follows area, so a thin far ribbon keeps its full strength. blade_on and blade_off: the burn at which the old white trail blade stops being drawn for a fighter, and the lower burn at which it comes back. bright_k: how a burn becomes strength (alpha = layer alpha x burn x bright_k, at most 1): the burn tops out at the cool term times the air, so a tier-4 burn of 0.7 needs more than 1 to be a full-strength trail. ramp_s: a point heats up to full strength over this long after the head lays it (0 is at once). pan_from, pan_to and pan_k: the ribbon dims to the share pan_k as the camera's speed across the world rises from pan_from to pan_to screen widths a second (1 is no dimming). head_cap_bh and head_len_bh: near the fighter's body the sheath is at most head_cap_bh body heights wide (the body and core in the layers' ratio), widening to its ceiling over head_len_bh body heights back along the path (Legal RL-222 (1): not a body-wide flame)."
